# Implementation Plan - Task Resumability & Retry Handler

Implement step-level job resumption and a user-facing retry mechanism for failed comic generation tasks. Since `api/internal/comic/pipeline.go` already persists intermediate pipeline state (`PipelineState`) in the database after every successful step and panel generation, resetting a failed job's status to `queued` will allow the background worker to resume execution seamlessly from the exact failed step without re-spending credits or re-generating completed panels.

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> - **No Extra Credit Consumption**: Retrying a failed job will NOT deduct additional user credits, as the credit was already reserved/consumed during initial job creation.
> - **Preserved State**: Retrying will retain all intermediate assets (narrative script, art direction, and generated panel images) in `generation_jobs.output` JSON. The worker will pick up at the recorded `state.Stage`.

## Open Questions

None. The existing pipeline state persistence structure supports resuming from any stage.

